index 0000000..bfbef05
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/ops/logging.md
@@ -0,0 +1,51 @@
+# Logging: archive, audit, alert
+
+Observability has three lanes. Pick the lane by **who needs to know and how
+fast**, not by severity alone.
+
+| Lane | Where | Use it for | Call |
+| ---- | ----- | ---------- | ---- |
+| **Archive** | `storage/logs/laravel-YYYY-MM-DD.log`, 14 days | Routine application logs, debug to error: diagnostics, handled exceptions, warnings. | `Log::info(...)`, `Log::error(...)` (default `stack` -> `daily`) |
+| **Audit** | `storage/logs/audit-YYYY-MM-DD.log`, 90 days, level `info`+ | Durable "who changed what / who tried what": membership role changes, subscription transitions, login lockouts. | `Log::channel('audit')->info('Subscription status changed', [...])` |
+| **Alert** | Discord incoming webhook | Actionable incidents worth waking someone up: a job that exhausted its retries, a payment-gateway webhook failing, a plan limit blocking an entity. | `app(\App\Ops\DiscordOpsAlert::class)->send($title, $message, $context)` |
+
+## Decision guide
+
+1. Does a human need to act **now**? -> **Alert** (and the code path usually
+   also writes an archive `error`).
+2. Will someone later ask "who did this / when / from what to what"? ->
+   **Audit**. Log ids and states, never secrets or raw PII.
+3. Otherwise -> **Archive**.
+
+A single event may use several lanes (e.g. a failed webhook: archive entry +
+alert). Don't alert on noise: every alert should have an owner and an action.
+
+## Rules
+
+- **Discord is not a log channel.** There is no `discord` channel in
+  `config/logging.php`, and none must be added. Alerts are an explicit call made
+  by code that decided the incident is page-worthy.
+- `DiscordOpsAlert::send()` never throws. A non-2xx answer or a transport error
+  is logged at `error` level in the archive, **without** the webhook URL (it
+  embeds the webhook token).
+- Payloads are redacted: context keys matching `password`, `token`, `secret`,
+  `authorization`, `api_key`/`api-key`/`apikey`, `webhook` and any string
+  containing `Bearer <credential>` become `[redacted]`; nested arrays are
+  redacted recursively and rendered as JSON. Still, don't pass secrets in.
+- The text (title, message, one `key=value` line per context entry) is cut to
+  1800 characters (Discord's limit is 2000).
+- No webhook configured (`DISCORD_WEBHOOK_URL` empty) means the call is a
+  silent no-op: no HTTP request. Local and test environments leave it empty.
+
+## Configuration
+
+| Env key | Default | Meaning |
+| ------- | ------- | ------- |
+| `LOG_STACK` | `daily` | Channels of the default `stack` (pinned to `daily` in `phpunit.xml`). |
+| `LOG_LEVEL` | `debug` | Minimum level of the archive channel. |
+| `LOG_DAILY_DAYS` | `14` | Archive retention in days. |
+| `LOG_AUDIT_LEVEL` | `info` | Minimum level of the audit channel. |
+| `LOG_AUDIT_DAYS` | `90` | Audit retention in days. |
+| `DISCORD_WEBHOOK_URL` | empty | Discord incoming webhook for ops alerts (`services.discord.webhook_url`). |
+
+Shipping logs to an external service is out of scope.
